# The sthost round's non-regression card: the row dispatch gains a layout (planes: a matrix's codes for every row and
# its block scales, two runs the file keeps wherever it keeps them), one tensor scale an expert applied once per output
# cell (every layout's, 1.0 for a type that reads none), and a table of file offsets beside a stack's bytes. On every
# layout that existed before, the added work is: one branch on the layout in `compute_rows`, one `Option` test of the
# offsets and one empty-slice pair in `ExpertStack::matrix`, two words and a float more in `PairWork`, per matrix cut
# about 10 ns; a token cuts 4 experts x 3 stacks x 57 layers = 684 of them, so 7 us; and one f32 multiply by 1.0 per
# output cell, at most 4 experts x (2 x 4096 + 4096) cells x 57 layers = 2.8 M cells a token at 1 ns, spread over
# the pool's 24+ workers: 0.12 ms worst case, on the compute that sits under the ~53 ms host-DRAM wall (rig-log
# plan.md 「흐름 모델」's 18.9 tok/s). Together at most 0.2 % and 0.013 % expected [derived from the code; no timed run
# behind it]. The planes arm itself is on no existing model's path. The band leaves room for what the derivation
# cannot close, the link layout of a rebuilt binary (a fixed first arm read 0.3-0.8 % slow before the runner rotated
# arm order).
kind: noninf
question: does the row dispatch with the planes layout wired in decode as fast as the base's, the changed arm no slower
  than the base by more than the margin?
term: bloomery-decode tok/s @ n = 96 (BLOOMERY_DECODE_N default), the runner's default prompt, the default reference
  profile, the A6000 box, changed tree vs base tree, interleaved in one lease, paired by round
unit: %
predict: -0.2..0.1
rounds: 8
sd: 0.6 % AGENTS.md 「Know the ruler」 same-binary scatter, the default
margin: 1.0 % the default: about the ruler's spread at 4-6 rounds; at 8 rounds the paired interval is 0.71 %, which
  the band's lower edge clears
condition: the lead's go, then from this tree with the base tree built beside it (`just build-decode` in both),
  BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/sthost-noninf.card' BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=8 just ab-decode
  <the base tree>; the runner rotates arm order every round, netdata is frozen under the lease, and no other compute
  runs on the box (the witness blocks open and close each round with the card name, clocks and Xid counters); a round
  with a [cold] or [other-busy] row is void
decide-in: the planes wiring costs nothing the ruler resolves: land it as it is
decide-below: re-derive the dispatch terms before landing: perf-record the changed arm (-e cpu-clock, cut with --time)
  and read `compute_rows` and `ExpertStack::matrix` first, since the added branches are the only code on the old path
decide-above: check arm identity and the link layout first (an A/A arm through BLOOMERY_AB_ENVS), then record the gain
  as noise; nothing in the change shortens a term of the old path
